  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ACCOUNTABLE INCLUSIVE EDUCATION IN PORT LOKO DISTRICT, NORTH-WEST SIERRA LEONE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to improve student learning outcomes in 20 underperforming senior secondary schools (10 schools in year 1 and 2 and a further 10 in years 2 and 3) by enabling more accountable and inclusive learning environments.  In the first year the project will directly target 10 principals, 10 vice-principals, over 350 teachers, Boards of Governors and community stakeholders. The main activities include training of school leadership, training of teachers including subject specific training, coaching/mentoring and the establishment of learning networks and communities of practice</narrative>
  </description>
